    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1229">

                <pb facs="0987" n="871" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg871"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6368/147.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Vice Consul Bevan to the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Tampico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-11">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 11, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Penn-Mex Oil Company and the Aguilar Petroleum Company have been closed down by
                    decree signed by Sub-Secretary of Fomento and authorized by First Chief of the
                    Constitutionalist Army.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bevan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
